ytic and computational search, discarded approaches, critic and red-team passes, numerical experiments, proof reconstruction, novelty checking, formalization of critical lemmas, independent replication, manuscript preparation, and publication-style revisions.\",\n    \"execution_shape\": \"A persistent multi-agent research program with parallel proposer, critic, verifier, literature, experiment, formalization, and editorial roles. Elapsed hours are wall-clock program duration, not aggregate worker-hours.\",\n    \"token_accounting\": \"Reasoning tokens include hidden deliberation or equivalent inference compute across proposer, critic, verifier, and retry calls. Input and output totals cover retrieval contexts, branch records, code, proof drafts, reviews, and manuscript artifacts.\",\n    \"cost_scope\": \"Total costs include model inference, retrieval infrastructure, licensed data where necessary, numerical and symbolic compute, theorem-prover integration, orchestration, storage, governance, verification, replication, and contingency for long-tail failed branches.\",\n    \"governance_cost_breakdown_usd\": {\n      \"identity_hashing_and_agent_provenance\": 45000,\n      \"budget_enforcement_and_rate_controls\": 90000,\n      \"branch_receipts_and_tamper_evident_logs\": 225000,\n      \"evidence_preservation_and_artifact_retention\": 280000,\n      \"policy_checks_and_release_gates\": 140000\n    },\n    \"verification_cost_breakdown_usd\": {\n      \"independent_proof_reconstruction\": 700000,\n      \"formalization_and_machine_checking_of_critical_components\": 550000,\n      \"independent_computational_replication\": 300000,\n      \"adversarial_review_and_referee_style_audit\": 300000\n    }\n  },\n  \"uncertainty_drivers\": [\n    \"Whether the target requires a fundamentally new analytic idea rather than refinement of known frameworks.\",\n    \"How much of the decisive proof can be represented reliably in current theorem provers.\",\n    \"The difficulty of turning numerical or asymptotic evidence into uniform rigorous bounds.\",\n    \"Sensitivity of the claimed threshold to constants, error terms, dimension ranges, and limiting arguments.\",\n    \"The rate at which model-generated branches produce genuinely distinct mathematics rather than correlated restatements.\",\n    \"Availability and machine readability of the relevant literature, auxiliary computations, and implicit expert knowledge.\",\n    \"Potential need for large optimization searches, interval arithmetic, or new certified numerical infrastructure.\",\n    \"Novelty requirements imposed by referees if a matching result is already known.\",\n    \"Context degradation, proof hallucination, and error correlation between nominally independent model critics.\",\n    \"Unpredictable manuscript revision cycles and requests for stronger generality or cleaner proofs.\"\n  ],\n  \"minimum_evidence\": [\n    \"A precise theorem statement matching the target regime, with all asymptotic quantifiers, constants, and dimension assumptions explicit.\",\n    \"A complete proof whose dependencies are traced to primary sources or proved within the project.\",\n    \"Independent line-by-line reconstruction by verifier instances that did not share the proposer transcript.\",\n    \"Machine-checked formalization of the most failure-prone inequalities, limit exchanges, optimization claims, and auxiliary lemmas, with any unformalized gap clearly delimited.\",\n    \"Reproducible code, fixed environments, seeds, input data, and certified outputs for every computational claim.\",\n    \"Independent reruns of numerical and symbolic experiments using a separately implemented pipeline.\",\n    \"Stress tests covering boundary cases, finite-dimension behavior, numerical conditioning, and asymptotic error accumulation.\",\n    \"A documented literature and priority search establishing whether the result is new, a reconstruction, or an alternative proof.\",\n    \"Adversarial referee-style reports and a resolution log for every substantive objection.\",\n    \"A submission-ready manuscript and archival package containing proof versions, branch provenance, computational certificates, and verification receipts.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"The required advance may depend on a conceptual insight that cannot be reached by scaling search or verification.\",\n    \"A model ensemble may exhibit correlated mathematical errors, invalidating apparent independent agreement.\",\n    \"Critical analytic steps may resist reliable formalization or certified numerical treatment.\",\n    \"The search space may be too diffuse for branch budgeting to preserve the rare productive direction.\",\n    \"A numerically convincing construction may fail to yield the uniform rigor required for publication.\",\n    \"The intended meaning of the Cohn\u2013Elkies threshold may require clarification of normalization, asymptotic regime, and exact matching criterion.\",\n    \"Access restrictions, incomplete sources, or undocumented computations may impede faithful reproduction.\",\n    \"The result may be independently rediscovered but judged insufficiently novel if a published proof already establishes the same bound.\",\n    \"Compute, context-window, or tool-reliability limits may force repeated proof compression and introduce hidden gaps.\",\n    \"No budget level can guarantee discovery of a new theorem; the high estimate primarily buys broader search and stronger verification rather than assured success.\"\n  ]\n}"
